  "limitations": [
    "The engines do not receive identical prompt or decode token IDs.",
    "The gem16 decode benchmark requires a positive initial context and therefore starts one position later than llama-bench tg128.",
    "Gem16 uses direct FP8 attention and checkpoint-FP8 K/V; llama.cpp maps source FP8 attention weights to Q8_0 and uses F16 K/V.",
    "Llama.cpp offloads 49/49 layers to CUDA0 but retains a 1,920 MiB CPU-mapped model buffer.",
    "llama-bench feeds synthetic random tokens and reports aggregate generation time; gem16 follows its deterministic generated sequence and also reports per-token latency.",
    "The result characterizes standardized short shapes and engine timing boundaries; it is not an exact semantic, format, or timing-boundary parity claim."
  ]
